'''Zam Wesell''' was a [[Clawdite]] [[Gender|female]] [[bounty hunter]] who lived during the [[Republic Era|waning years]] of the [[Galactic Republic]]. As a Clawdite, Wesell possessed the ability to physically [[Changeling|alter]] her appearance&mdash;a power which she usually utilized to assume the visage of a [[human]] female. Prior to the [[First Battle of Geonosis|beginning]] of the [[Clone Wars]], the [[bounty]] hunter [[Jango Fett]] enlisted Wesell's aid to [[Plot to assassinate Senator Amidala|assassinate]] [[Senator]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] of [[Naboo]] in [[22 BBY]]. Her efforts ultimately failed, however, resulting in Wesell's [[death]] at the hands of Fett before she could identify him as the would-be [[assassin]] to Amidala's [[Jedi]] [[bodyguard]]s.

==Biography==
===Early life and career===
{{Quote|That's enough. Do that thing we did on Snugano.''"<br />"''I nearly died that day.|Jango Fett and Zam Wesell|<ref name="Wesell Run">{{InsiderCite|209|Galactic Tales: The Wesell Run}}</ref>}}
A [[Clawdite]] [[Gender|female]], Zam Wesell was [[Reproduction|born]] on the [[planet]] [[Zolan]]. [[Gender|She]] was trained by the [[Mabari]] until she desired wealth and journeyed to [[Denon]] to employ her skills and training as an [[assassin]]. At some point, Wesell started to work with [[bounty hunter]] [[Jango Fett]],<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> becoming his frequent partner.<ref name="Secrets of the Bounty Hunters">''[[Star Wars: The Secrets of the Bounty Hunters]]''</ref> During an incident where she worked with Fett on [[Snugano]], she nearly died.<ref name="Wesell Run" />

===''Halcyon'' vacation===
{{Quote|Took you long enough, Zam.''"<br />"''I had to get my bets in on the predavorexx.''"<br />"''Knew I should have partnered with Jango Fett instead. He has a better sense of humor.|Aurra Sing and Wesell|<ref name="Halcyon Legacy 2">[[Halcyon Legacy 2|''Halcyon Legacy'' 2]]</ref>}}
[[File:ZamWesellWeequay-HalcyonLegacy2.png|thumb|right|250px|Zam disguised as a Weequay]]
Prior to [[22 BBY]],<ref name="Halcyon Legacy 2 date">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the events of [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']] to the year [[22 BBY]]. Because the death of Zam Wesell is depicted in that film, and a living Wesell appears in flashbacks in [[Halcyon Legacy 2|''Halcyon Legacy'' 2]], those flashbacks must have taken place before 22 BBY.</ref> Wesell went on a vacation with [[Aurra Sing]] aboard the ''[[Halcyon]]'' disguised as a human female. While on on board, they were hired by [[Colram Vestig]] to protect himself, and his son, [[Wilmar]], from the [[Hutt Clan|Hutts]]. When Wilmar was kidnapped by Weequays employed by the Hutts, Sing and Wesell went to [[Numidian Prime]] to [[Rescue of Wilmar|rescue him]]. While there, Sing was attacked by a [[Predavorexx]]. After defeating the beast, Wesell disguised herself as one of the Hutts' [[Weequay]] guards and helped Sing take out the remaining guards to save Wilmar. The duo were then able to return the boy to his father on the ''Halycon.''<ref name="Halcyon Legacy 2" />

===Assassination plot and death===
{{Quote|Who hired you? Tell us. Tell us now!''"<br />"''It was a bounty hunter called&mdash;''"<br />"''Wee shahnit&hellip; sleemo.|Anakin Skywalker, and Zam Wesell, shortly before the latter's death|<ref name="Episode II" />}}
[[File:ZamWesell-SWZ.png|thumb|left|250px|Zam Wesell disguised as a human while on Coruscant]]
In 22 BBY,<ref name="Timelines" /> Wesell was hired by Fett to [[Plot to assassinate Senator Amidala|assassinate]] [[Naboo]] [[Senator]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] to prevent her from speaking up against the [[Military Creation Act]]. Sometime later, Wesell bombed the Senator's [[J-type diplomatic barge|cruiser]] when it reached [[Coruscant]]. However, Amidala herself wasn't on the [[cruiser]]. Instead, it was her [[Naboo Royal Handmaidens|handmaiden]], [[Cordé]]. After receiving the news, Wesell told Fett that she had bombed the ship, but she used a decoy. Fett then gave her some [[kouhun]]s and told her to be careful while holding them as they were very [[poison]]ous. Wesell sent a [[ASN courier droid|droid]] to do it for her, but two [[Jedi]] had been assigned to protect the senator: [[Jedi Knight]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and his [[Padawan]] [[Anakin Skywalker]]. Skywalker quickly [[Death|killed]] the kouhuns and Kenobi grabbed the droid. While the droid was speeding through an express way, Wesell shot it with [[KiSteer 1284 projectile rifle|her KiSteer 1284 projectile rifle]] which caused Kenobi to start falling through Coruscant's [[atmosphere]].<ref name="Episode II" />

[[File:Koro-2.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Zam Wesell being chased by Jedi Anakin Skywalker and Obi-Wan Kenobi]]
Wesell quickly fled in her [[Koro-2 all-environment Exodrive airspeeder|speeder]] but the Jedi were able to pursue her with a commandeered open-top [[XJ-6 airspeeder]]. Wesell took her speeder on a nosedive—plunging 2,670 [[meter]]s toward the lower levels of [[Corusca Circus]]. With the Jedi relentlessly pursuing her, Wesell flew through the exhaust flames of the [[Kerdos Company recycling plant]], hoping that the flames would scorch her adversaries in the open-top speeder. Seeing the pair still chasing her and unharmed by the flames, Wesell fired at the couplings of a nearby electrical plant, causing the Jedi's speeder to be inundated by electrical shock. The bounty hunter then steered her craft into a network of tunnels, aiming once again to lose the pursuing Jedi. Skywalker did not chase directly into tunnel, but opted to travel an alternate route. Wesell wove through tunnels, reaching speeds of 400 [[Kilometer per hour|kilometers per hour]]. Upon exiting the network at the [[Cybot Galactica]] droid research institute, the bounty hunter was surprised when Skywalker suddenly jumped on top of her airspeeder. During a struggle to get Skywalker off her speeder, Wesell briefly [[Changeling|shapeshifted]] into her Clawdite form which caused Skywalker to realize she was a changeling species. The Jedi ignited [[Anakin Skywalker's first lightsaber|his lightsaber]] and sliced at the windscreen, knocking out the guidance systems. Wesell used her [[KYD-21 blaster pistol]] and shot the [[lightsaber]] out of Skywalker's hand, but the ensuing struggle caused Wesell to misfire her blaster pistol, damaging the control pipes.<ref name="Episode II" />

[[File:Clawdite.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Wesell reverted to her Clawdite form as she lay dying.]]
After crashing her speeder into [[Vos Gesal Street]] in the [[Uscru Entertainment District]], Wesell was able to flee into the [[Outlander Club]]. Skywalker was about to dash in but Kenobi reminded his Padawan that Wesell had gone in to hide, not to run. Once inside the club, Skywalker told Kenobi he knew that Wesell was a changeling and that she was a female. Kenobi said they should be extra careful in searching for her. As the pair went their separate ways with Skywalker looking for Wesell and Kenobi getting a drink, Wesell approached Kenobi from behind and attempted to shoot him, but Kenobi sensed her and [[Dismemberment|chopped]] her [[Limb|arm]] off with his [[Obi-Wan Kenobi's second lightsaber|lightsaber]]. Wesell screamed in pain and fell to the ground. Kenobi and Skywalker carried Wesell outside and asked her if she knew who she was trying to kill. Wesell answered that she knew it was a Senator from Naboo. Then she was asked who hired her but, Wesell answered that it was merely a job as she was reluctant to reveal her employer's name. Skywalker then pressured her to tell them and Wesell was about to say who it was when Fett, who had been watching the whole interrogation, shot her in the neck with a [[Kamino saberdart]]. Wesell then said her final words, cursing at Fett in [[Huttese]] and died shortly after.<ref name="Episode II" />

[[Standard decade|Decade]]s later, Wesell was mentioned in the ''[[Galactic Explorer's Guide]]'', a survival guide written by [[Hondo Ohnaka]] and [[DK-RA-43]].<ref name="Galactic Explorer's Guide">''[[Star Wars: The Galactic Explorer's Guide]]''</ref>

==Personality and traits==
[[File:ZamWesell-SWBC64.png|thumb|right|220px|Zam in her human form aiming her KYD-21 blaster pistol]]
{{Quote|Wee shahnit&hellip;sleemo.|Zam Wesell's last words|<ref name="Episode II" />}}
Wesell preferred to strike her targets from afar, utilizing long-range [[sniper rifle]]s or remote [[probe droid]]s.<ref name="USW" /> Wesell used her [[changeling]] powers to take on the form of a [[human]] [[Gender|female]] and kept this form while hiding from the Jedi in the [[Outlander Club]]. When captured and interrogated by [[Jedi Knight]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and his [[Padawan]] [[Anakin Skywalker]], Wesell refused to give the names of her employers, but upon being pressured by Skywalker, Wesell was about to give in to the Jedi's demands, only for her partner [[Jango Fett]] to kill her before she could reveal the names of their employers.<ref name="Episode II" />

==Powers and abilities==
{{Quote|I think 'he' is a 'she'. And I think she is a changeling.|Anakin Skywalker, to Obi-Wan Kenobi|<ref name="Episode II" />}}
As a changeling, she was able to assume the appearance of anyone she chose, including her targets.<ref name="USW" /> She was capable of taking on any [[humanoid]] form.<ref name="Databank" /> As she died, she reverted from speaking [[Galactic Basic Standard]] to [[Clawdite (language)|Clawdite]],<ref name="Language">{{SWKidsYouTube|series=Star Wars By the Numbers|text=Every Language in Star Wars Movies|video=CZp8Civk2co|nolive=1}}</ref> before cursing Jango Fett in [[Huttese]].<ref name="Helmet Collection 39">{{HelmetCollectionCite|39|Helmets}}</ref> She was also a skilled markswoman<ref name="Episode II" /> and pilot.<ref name="Jedi Knights 4">[[Jedi Knights 4|''Jedi Knights'' 4]]</ref>

==Equipment==
[[File:KiSteer1284ProjectileRifle-SWBC64.png|thumb|left|300px|Wesell's KiSteer 1284 projectile rifle]]
Wesell made use of a variety of gear in her profession as a bounty hunter and [[assassin]] and always tried to have the best arsenal available. Her helmet utilized retractable [[macrobinoculars]] to extend her range of vision and had an attached scarf to further hide her appearance. She wore an elastic mesh body suit that adjusted to her changes in shape, over which she wore armored [[gauntlet]]s, shin guards and [[boot]]s. The suit incorporated a breathing system that allowed air to be directly pumped into her lungs through tubes affixed to her rib cage. She also wore an [[impact energy skirt]] that collected power. The entire outfit, including the pin on her cloak, was inscribed with emblems
and [[Mabari script|script]] of the [[Mabari]], an order of warrior-knights who trained her.<ref name="Bust Collection">{{BustCollectionCite|64|Character}}</ref>

[[File:Koro2ExodriveAirspeeder-SWBC64.png|thumb|right|250px|Wesell's personal ''Koro-2'' Exodrive speeder.]]
For transportation, Wesell often stole vehicles to prevent her being directly tracked. Sometimes she preferred her personal [[Koro-2 all-environment exodrive airspeeder|''Koro-2'' Exodrive]] [[airspeeder]], a forked, green, extremely fast speeder that was difficult to handle but
designed for any environment, no matter how hostile. Wesell's arsenal consisted of a [[KiSteer 1284 projectile rifle]] for long-range attacks and a [[Hadrium alloy|Hadrian alloy]] [[KYD-21 blaster pistol|KYD-21 blaster]] for close quarters combat.<ref name="Bust Collection" /> She also was known to make use of [[ASN courier droid]]s.<ref name="Episode II" />

==Behind the scenes==
Zam Wesell first appeared in ''Attack of the Clones'' played by [[Leeanna Walsman]].<ref name="Episode II" /> [[Star Wars Jedi Master Magazine 2|''Star Wars Jedi Master'' Magazine 2]] erroneously states she died in [[32 BBY]].<ref name="JMM2">[[Star Wars Jedi Master Magazine 2|''Star Wars Jedi Master'' Magazine 2]]</ref>

